{"kind":"FETCH","data":{"headers":{},"body":"{\"id\":33695,\"title\":\"Growing Up Twisted\",\"tagline\":\"\",\"overview\":\"Growing Up Twisted is an American reality television series that premiered on A&E on July 27, 2010. The show follows the life of Twisted Sister vocalist Dee Snider, his wife Suzette to whom he's been married since October 21, 1981, and their four children, Jesse, Shane, Cody, and Cheyenne. The show is similar to Gene Simmons Family Jewels in that it follows a rock star and his family through their everyday lives. Season one ran from July 27, 2010 until August 24, 2010.\",\"posterPath\":null,\"backdropPath\":null,\"youtubeBackdrop\":\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/otWwgOlDSxc/maxresdefault.jpg\",\"anilistBanner\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"year\":2010,\"genres\":[],\"status\":\"Ended\",\"type\":\"tv\",\"totalSeasons\":1,\"totalEpisodes\":7,\"createdBy\":[],\"networks\":[\"A&E\"],\"countries\":[{\"code\":\"US\",\"name\":\"US\"}],\"lastAirDate\":\"2010-08-24\",\"cast\":[{\"id\":60434,\"name\":\"Dee Snider\",\"character\":\"Unknown\",\"photo\":\"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/qoWLyZs31jmm2TrknO4EsG8HV9S.jpg\"},{\"id\":1240470,\"name\":\"Jesse Blaze Snider\",\"character\":\"Unknown\",\"photo\":null}],\"trailers\":[{\"key\":\"otWwgOlDSxc\",\"name\":\"Official Trailer\",\"site\":\"YouTube\",\"type\":\"Trailer\"},{\"key\":\"DpSPLmSt37k\",\"name\":\"Official Trailer\",\"site\":\"YouTube\",\"type\":\"Trailer\"},{\"key\":\"rZ7pjhYxAUk\",\"name\":\"Official Trailer\",\"site\":\"YouTube\",\"type\":\"Trailer\"}],\"similar\":[],\"seasonNumber\":1,\"seasonName\":\"Season 1\",\"seasonOverview\":\"\",\"seasonPoster\":null,\"seasonAirDate\":\"2010-07-27\",\"episodes\":[{\"number\":0,\"name\":\"Baptism By Snider\",\"overview\":\"Twisted Sister lead singer, Dee Snider, is the lone voice of reason when his family packs a whirlwind of activity into one week. Their eldest son, Jesse, wants to have a christening for his daughter, but a touching tribute song he writes for the event opens up old wounds between father and son. Then the family heads to the city for son Shane's stand-up act, but his brother Cody nearly gets into a fight with a comic that disrespects the Snider clan. Finally, the family needs to pull it all together in time to stage a very touching... and very twisted christening.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2010-07-27\",\"runtime\":0},{\"number\":1,\"name\":\"Carpet and Drapes\",\"overview\":\"Dee decides to get his \\\"Suzette Forever\\\" tattoo redone as a surprise on their anniversary, but is floored to find out that Suzette started the process of removing her \\\"Dee Forever\\\" tattoo. After this ruins their anniversary dinner, Suzette is on a mission to fix things with Dee and designs a new tattoo that she later seductively reveals. Throughout the anniversary plans, the kids realize they've gotten to learn a little \\\"too much information\\\" about their parent's sex life, especially when they find a packet of pink hair dye not intended for their mom's locks.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2010-07-27\",\"runtime\":0},{\"number\":2,\"name\":\"Are Those Real?\",\"overview\":\"Shane announces to the family that they all need to help him shoot his sketch, \\\"My Friend Poseidon,\\\" for his final improv class with each member of the family taking an important role in the execution. The project hits an unexpected bump when a clerk at the costume store insults Suzette's physique and the Snider boys seek justice. And mother and daughter have a sparring match to exert some pent up aggression with one another, which ends in a bloody mess.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2010-08-03\",\"runtime\":0},{\"number\":3,\"name\":\"Empty Nest\",\"overview\":\"When her son Jesse reprimands her for trying to pierce his daughter's ears, Suzette decides the real issue is that she is starting to feel some empty nest syndrome. She urges Dee to reverse his vasectomy and visits her doctor only to find out they won't be able to have more children. Dee and Suzette begin to explore adoption but a surprise visit from a social worker from Child Protective Services shatters the couple's dream to adopt.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2010-08-03\",\"runtime\":0},{\"number\":4,\"name\":\"I Still Wanna Rock\",\"overview\":\"Dee gets a last minute call to perform in Atlantic City and decides it should be a family affair. While Suzette is ready to party and hits the casino floor with sons Shane and Cody, Dee invites Jesse and Cheyenne to perform. Jess performs \\\"Rock n' Roll Ain't Dead\\\" at the show and Cheyenne sings \\\"Cherry Bomb\\\" with the legendary Lita Ford, both wowing the crowd.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2010-08-10\",\"runtime\":0},{\"number\":5,\"name\":\"Uneasy Riders\",\"overview\":\"The family rides motorcycles for a charity event; Dee and Suzette fight over Jesse's participation.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2010-08-17\",\"runtime\":0},{\"number\":6,\"name\":\"Mommy's Boys\",\"overview\":\"Suzette meddles in the romantic affairs of both boys.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"2010-08-24\",\"runtime\":0}],\"firstAirDate\":\"2010-07-27\"}","status":200,"url":""},"revalidate":86400,"tags":[]}